-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M16 7h6v6\"></path><path d=\"m22 7-8.5 8.5-5-5L2 17\"></path></svg>Salary</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/tax-data\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Data</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/widgets\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-code-xml h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m18 16 4-4-4-4\"></path><path d=\"m6 8-4 4 4 4\"></path><path d=\"m14.5 4-5 16\"></path></svg>Widgets</a></nav><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><a class=\"hidden sm:flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-600 to-emerald-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/20 hover:shadow-emerald-500/30 transition-all hover:scale-[1.02]\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Calculate Now</a><button data-slot=\"button\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium transition-all disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 shrink-0 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive hover:bg-accent dark:hover:bg-accent/50 h-8 rounded-md gap-1.5 px-3 has-[&gt;svg]:px-2.5 lg:hidden text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground\" aria-label=\"Toggle mobile menu\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-menu h-5 w-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 12h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 18h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 6h16\"></path></svg></button></div></div></header><main id=\"main-content\" class=\"flex-1\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/paycheck-difference-calculator#software\",\"@type\":\"WebApplication\",\"name\":\"Paycheck Difference Calculator\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/paycheck-difference-calculator\",\"applicationCategory\":\"FinanceApplication\",\"operatingSystem\":\"Web\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":0,\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"availability\":\"https://schema.org/InStock\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/paycheck-difference-calculator\"},\"description\":\"Calculate the difference in take-home pay between two states or salaries. Free 2026 calculator for all 50 states.\",\"provider\":{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/#organization\"},\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Rachel Mitchell\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/about#rachel-mitchell\",\"jobTitle\":\"Lead Tax Analyst & Editorial Director, CPA\",\"description\":\"Rachel Mitchell is a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) licensed in Illinois with over 12 years of experience in individual and small-business taxation. She specializes in federal and state income tax compliance, FICA optimization, payroll tax strategy, and multi-state tax planning. Rachel holds an MS in Taxation from Golden Gate University and a BS in Accounting from the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. She is an active member of the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA) and the Illinois CPA Society. Before joining TheTaxCalc, Rachel spent 8 years at a Big Four accounting firm advising high-net-worth clients on tax-efficient wealth strategies.\",\"knowsAbout\":[\"Federal Income Tax\",\"State Income Tax\",\"FICA Tax\",\"Payroll Tax\",\"IRS Compliance\",\"Tax Planning\",\"Multi-State Taxation\",\"Tax-Advantaged Accounts\"],\"sameAs\":[\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/rachelmitchellcpa/\",\"https://www.aicpa-cima.com/\"],\"worksFor\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},\"image\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/author-rachel-mitchell.webp\"}},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/paycheck-difference-calculator#faq\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How much difference does state tax make on my paycheck?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"It can be dramatic. If you earn $75,000, living in Texas (0% state tax) instead of California (up to 9.3% at that bracket) saves you roughly $5,000–$7,000 per year in state taxes alone. Moving from Illinois (4.95%) to Texas saves about $3,500 per year at the same salary. Our calculator shows you the exact dollar difference for any salary and state pair.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Which states have no income tax?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Nine states levy no personal income tax: Alaska, Florida, Nevada, New Hampshire, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Washington, and Wyoming. New Hampshire taxes dividend and interest income but not wages. If you live in any of these states, your paycheck only shrinks due to federal tax and FICA — no state tax is withheld.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do I compare my paycheck if I move to a different state?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Enter your current salary and state as the first scenario, then add a second scenario with the same salary and your new state. The calculator will show your after-tax take-home pay for both, plus the exact difference. You can also adjust the salary if the move comes with a raise or pay cut.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does this account for local or city taxes?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes, for New York City residents. If you select New York state and enable the NYC Resident toggle, the calculator includes the city income tax (3.078%–3.876%). Most other cities do not levy local income taxes, but if they do, you would need to factor those in separately.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What about FICA — does that change by state?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"No. FICA taxes — 6.2% for Social Security (up to the $184,500 wage base in 2026) and 1.45% for Medicare — are federal and do not vary by state. Everyone pays the same FICA regardless of where they live. The only FICA variation is the 0.9% Additional Medicare Tax on income over $200,000.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can I see the difference in bi-weekly or monthly take-home pay?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. The comparison table shows net take-home pay annually, monthly, and bi-weekly for each scenario. The difference column applies to each time period, so you can see exactly how much more or less each paycheck would be.\"}}]},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/paycheck-difference-calculator#breadcrumb\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Paycheck Difference Calculator\"}]}]}</script><nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"mb-6 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><a class=\"underline underline-offset-2 decoration-muted-foreground/40 hover:decoration-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors flex items-center gap-1\" href=\"/\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-house h-3.5 w-3.5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M15 21v-8a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-4a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v8\"></path><path d=\"M3 10a2 2 0 0 1 .709-1.528l7-5.999a2 2 0 0 1 2.582 0l7 5.999A2 2 0 0 1 21 10v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z\"></path></svg><span class=\"hidden sm:inline\">Home</span></a><span class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5 text-muted-foreground\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"></path></svg><span class=\"text-foreground font-medium\">Paycheck Difference Calculator</span></span></nav><div class=\"mb-10 text-center\"><div class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 border border-blue-500/20 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-blue-400 mb-6\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right-left h-3.5 w-3.5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m16 3 4 4-4 4\"></path><path d=\"M20 7H4\"></path><path d=\"m8 21-4-4 4-4\"></path><path d=\"M4 17h16\"></path></svg>State-by-State</div><h1 class=\"text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-5xl\">Paycheck Difference<!-- --> <span class=\"gradient-text\">Calculator</span></h1><p class=\"mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">See exactly how much your take-home pay changes when you move states, change jobs, or adjust deductions. Real numbers, no guesswork.</p></div><section class=\"mb-10 rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6 text-center\">How It <span class=\"gradient-text\">Works</span></h2><div class=\"grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3\"><div class=\"text-center\"><div class=\"inline-flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 font-bold text-lg mb-3\">1</div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\">Enter Your Paycheck</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Input your current salary, state, and filing status as the baseline.</p></div><div class=\"text-center\"><div class=\"inline-flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 font-bold text-lg mb-3\">2</div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\">Add a Comparison</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Add another scenario with a different state, salary, or deductions.</p></div><div class=\"text-center\"><div class=\"inline-flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 font-bold text-lg mb-3\">3</div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\">See the Difference</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">The difference column shows exactly how much more or less you take home.</p></div></div></section><section class=\"mb-10\"><div id=\"scenario-comparison\" class=\"scroll-mt-24\"><div data-state=\"closed\" data-slot=\"collapsible\"><div data-slot=\"card\" class=\"text-card-foreground flex flex-col gap-6 rounded-xl border py-6 shadow-sm border-blue-500/20 bg-card/80 backdrop-blur-sm\"><div data-slot=\"collapsible-trigger\" class=\"@container/card-header grid auto-rows-min grid-rows-[auto_auto] items-start gap-1.5 px-6 has-data-[slot=card-action]:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] [.border-b]:pb-6 cursor-pointer pb-4 transition-colors hover:bg-muted/30\" type=\"button\" aria-controls=\"radix-_R_5av5uhtb_\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-state=\"closed\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right-left h-5 w-5 text-blue-400\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m16 3 4 4-4 4\"></path><path d=\"M20 7H4\"></path><path d=\"m8 21-4-4 4-4\"></path><path d=\"M4 17h16\"></path></svg><div data-slot=\"card-title\" class=\"font-semibold text-lg\">Compare Tax Scenarios</div><span data-slot=\"badge\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md border px-2 py-0.5 font-medium w-fit whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 [&amp;&gt;svg]:size-3 gap-1 [&amp;&gt;svg]:pointer-events-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive transition-[color,box-shadow] overflow-hidden [a&amp;]:hover:bg-accent [a&amp;]:hover:text-accent-foreground text-xs border-blue-500/30 text-blue-400\">New</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground transition-transform\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></div><div data-slot=\"card-description\" class=\"text-muted-foreground text-sm\">Compare up to 4 scenarios side by side — different states, 401(k) contributions, or filing statuses</div></div><div data-state=\"closed\" id=\"radix-_R_5av5uhtb_\" hidden=\"\" data-slot=\"collapsible-content\"></div></div></div></div></section><section class=\"mb-10 space-y-6\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground\">How State Taxes Affect Your <span class=\"gradient-text\">Paycheck</span></h2><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Your paycheck is not just your salary minus federal taxes. State income tax can take another 0% to 13.3% off the top, depending on where you live. For someone earning $75,000, that means a difference of up to $10,000 in annual take-home pay between the highest-tax and lowest-tax states. Our paycheck difference calculator lets you see the exact dollar impact of state taxes, filing status changes, and pre-tax deductions side by side, so you know precisely what you gain or lose by moving or changing your withholding.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">The gap between states is widening. California charges up to 13.3% in state income tax, Hawaii up to 11%, and Oregon up to 9.9%. Meanwhile, nine states — Texas, Florida, Washington, Nevada, Wyoming, Alaska, South Dakota, Tennessee, and New Hampshire — charge zero personal income tax on wages. If you earn $100,000 and move from California to Texas, you keep roughly $10,000 more per year without changing your salary. That is the power of state tax policy on your paycheck, and it is exactly what this calculator is designed to reveal.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">But state tax is only part of the story. Pre-tax deductions like 401(k) contributions ($24,500 limit in 2026) and HSA contributions ($4,150 for individuals) reduce your taxable income at the federal and state level. By maximizing these deductions, you can lower your effective tax rate significantly. Our calculator lets you adjust 401(k) and HSA amounts independently for each scenario, so you can model the full impact of deductions on your take-home pay across different states and salary levels.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Every calculation uses the 2026 federal tax brackets, the $16,100 standard deduction for single filers, the $184,500 Social Security wage base, and the latest published state income tax rates from all 50 state revenue departments. Whether you are comparing a move from Illinois to Texas, evaluating a raise, or simply curious how much state tax costs you, this calculator gives you accurate, instant results.</p></section><section class=\"mb-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6\">Paycheck Difference <span class=\"gradient-text\">FAQ</span></h2><div class=\"space-y-3\"><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">How much difference does state tax make on my paycheck?</h3><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">It can be dramatic. If you earn $75,000, living in Texas (0% state tax) instead of California (up to 9.3% at that bracket) saves you roughly $5,000–$7,000 per year in state taxes alone. Moving from Illinois (4.95%) to Texas saves about $3,500 per year at the same salary. Our calculator shows you the exact dollar difference for any salary and state pair.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Which states have no income tax?</h3><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Nine states levy no personal income tax: Alaska, Florida, Nevada, New Hampshire, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Washington, and Wyoming. New Hampshire taxes dividend and interest income but not wages. If you live in any of these states, your paycheck only shrinks due to federal tax and FICA — no state tax is withheld.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">How do I compare my paycheck if I move to a different state?</h3><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Enter your current salary and state as the first scenario, then add a second scenario with the same salary and your new state. The calculator will show your after-tax take-home pay for both, plus the exact difference. You can also adjust the salary if the move comes with a raise or pay cut.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Does this account for local or city taxes?</h3><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Yes, for New York City residents. If you select New York state and enable the NYC Resident toggle, the calculator includes the city income tax (3.078%–3.876%). Most other cities do not levy local income taxes, but if they do, you would need to factor those in separately.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">What about FICA — does that change by state?</h3><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">No. FICA taxes — 6.2% for Social Security (up to the $184,500 wage base in 2026) and 1.45% for Medicare — are federal and do not vary by state. Everyone pays the same FICA regardless of where they live. The only FICA variation is the 0.9% Additional Medicare Tax on income over $200,000.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Can I see the difference in bi-weekly or monthly take-home pay?</h3><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Yes. The comparison table shows net take-home pay annually, monthly, and bi-weekly for each scenario. The difference column applies to each time period, so you can see exactly how much more or less each paycheck would be.</div></details></div></section><section class=\"mb-10 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-8 text-center\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">Related Calculators</h2><div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\">Paycheck Calculator</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\" href=\"/salary-comparison-calculator\">Salary Comparison</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\" href=\"/job-offer-comparison-calculator\">Job Offer Comparison</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\" href=\"/compare\">Compare States</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-all\" href=\"/salary\">Salary After Tax</a></div></section><section class=\"py-12 border-t border-border/20\"><section aria-label=\"Author: Rachel Mitchell\" class=\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-500/5 to-card/80 p-5 sm:p-6\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-4\"><img src=\"https://thetaxcalc.com/author-rachel-mitchell.webp\" alt=\"Rachel Mitchell, CPA\" width=\"48\" height=\"48\" class=\"h-12 w-12 shrink-0 rounded-full object-cover ring-1 ring-emerald-500/30\" loading=\"lazy\"/><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2\"><a class=\"text-base font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-emerald-400 transition-colors\" href=\"/about#rachel-mitchell\">Rachel Mitchell</a><span class=\"inline-flex items-center rounded-md bg-emerald-500/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-400 ring-1 ring-emerald-500/25\">CPA</span></div><p class=\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Lead Tax Analyst &amp; Editorial Director<!-- -->, TheTaxCalc</p><p class=\"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground line-clamp-2\">Rachel Mitchell is a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) licensed in Illinois with over 12 years of experience in individual and small-business taxation. She specializes in federal and state income tax compliance, FICA optimization, payroll tax strategy, and multi-state tax planning. Rachel holds an MS in Taxation from Golden Gate University and a BS in Accounting from the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. She is an active member of the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA) and the Illinois CPA Society. Before joining TheTaxCalc, Rachel spent 8 years at a Big Four accounting firm advising high-net-worth clients on tax-efficient wealth strategies.</p><div class=\"mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1\"><svg class=\"h-3 w-3 text-emerald-500/60\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M6.75 3v2.25M17.25 3v2.25M3 18.75V7.5a2.25 2.25 0 012.25-2.25h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 7.5v11.25m-18 0A2.25 2.25 0 005.25 21h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0021 18.75m-18 0v-7.5A2.25 2.25 0 015.25 9h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 11.25v7.5\"></path></svg>Reviewed: January 2026</span><span>Tax data verified against IRS Publication 15-T &amp; state revenue departments</span></div></div></div></section></section></div><!--$--><!--/$--></main><footer class=\"mt-auto border-t border-border/30 glass-strong\"><div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-500/5 via-emerald-500/10 to-emerald-500/5 border-b border-border/20\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><div class=\"flex flex-col items-center gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:justify-between\"><div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-foreground\">Stay Updated on <span class=\"text-emerald-400\">Tax Changes</span></h2><p class=\"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Get the latest tax tips, calculator updates, and financial insights delivered to your inbox.</p></div><div class=\"flex w-full max-w-sm gap-2\"><input type=\"email\" data-slot=\"input\" class=\"file:text-foreground selection:bg-primary selection:text-primary-foreground dark:bg-input/30 flex h-9 w-full min-w-0 rounded-md border px-3 py-1 text-base shadow-xs transition-[color,box-shadow] outline-none file:inline-flex file:h-7 file:border-0 file:bg-transparent file:text-sm file:font-medium disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50 md:text-sm focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive bg-background/50 border-border/30 placeholder:text-muted-foreground\" aria-label=\"Email address for newsletter\" placeholder=\"Enter your email\" value=\"\"/><button data-slot=\"button\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium transition-all disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive shadow-xs hover:bg-primary/90 h-9 px-4 py-2 has-[&gt;svg]:px-3 bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-600 to-emerald-500 text-white hover:from-emerald-500 hover:to-emerald-400 shrink-0\">Subscribe</button></div></div></div></div><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><div class=\"grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4\"><div class=\"space-y-4\"><a class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 transition-opacity hover:opacity-90\" href=\"/\"><div class=\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-500 to-emerald-600 shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/20\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-dollar-sign h-4 w-4 text-white\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><line x1=\"12\" x2=\"12\" y1=\"2\" y2=\"22\"></line><path d=\"M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6\"></path></svg></div><span class=\"text-lg font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground\">TheTaxCalc<span class=\"gradient-text\">.com</span></span></a><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Precision tax calculators for 2026. Compute your take-home pay, plan your mortgage, and compare state taxes — all free, all accurate.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 text-xs text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 px-2.5 py-1 text-emerald-400\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-shield h-3 w-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z\"></path></svg>2026 Tax Data</span><span class=\"flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full bg-muted/30 px-2.5 py-1\">Secure &amp; Private</span></div></div><div><h3 class=\"mb-4 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-foreground\">Calculators</h3><ul class=\"space-y-2\"><li><a class=\"flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-2 decoration-border/50 transition-colors hover:text-emerald-400 hover:decoration-emerald-400\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucid